# 4. OBJECT STRUCTURE UNDERSTANDING AND GROUPING

Stagecraft should understand the structure of imported objects, not just characters.

For any imported 3D asset, inspect its:

- Mesh hierarchy.
- Groups.
- Parent nodes.
- Child nodes.
- Materials.
- Skeletons.
- Bones.
- Animation groups.
- Named components.

Display these in an expandable hierarchy.

### Highlight and selection

Allow me to:

- Highlight an individual mesh.
- Highlight an entire group.
- Highlight a parent structure.
- Select multiple structures.
- Select all children of a node.
- Select an entire hierarchy.
- Isolate a structure.
- Hide a structure.
- Lock a structure.

### Grouping

Implement proper grouping and ungrouping.

I should be able to select multiple structures and combine them into a logical group.

For example:

Character
- Head Group
- Upper Body Group
- Left Arm Group
- Right Arm Group
- Lower Body Group

I should also be able to create custom groups.

Support:
- Group.
- Ungroup.
- Parent.
- Unparent.
- Attach.
- Detach.
- Merge where technically appropriate.
- Duplicate group.
- Rename group.
- Lock group.
- Hide group.

### Non-destructive operations

Do not destroy the original mesh or rig when grouping.

Distinguish between:
- Logical grouping.
- Parenting.
- Mesh merging.
- Material merging.
- Skeletal attachment.

Provide appropriate operations for each.

Maintain undo and redo support.

