# 15. REQUIRED ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Do not mark this phase complete until these interactions have been tested.

### Test 1 — Hover mapping

Import a compatible humanoid character.

Hover over its head, arms, elbows, hands, legs and feet.

Verify that the correct structure highlights and is identified.

### Test 2 — Normal selection

Single-click the character.

Verify that the normal transformation controls appear.

Move, rotate and scale it.

### Test 3 — Articulated editing

Double-click the character.

Select the left arm.

Drag the rotation handle.

Verify that the arm rotates around the shoulder and remains attached.

Select the forearm.

Rotate it around the elbow.

Verify that the upper arm and shoulder remain correctly connected.

### Test 4 — Joint preservation

Create multiple poses.

Switch between them.

Verify that no mesh detaches, no hierarchy is corrupted and no joint suddenly jumps.

### Test 5 — Object grouping

Select multiple objects or mesh structures.

Group them.

Move the group.

Ungroup them.

Verify that their original transforms and relationships are preserved.

### Test 6 — Keyframes

Create keyframes for different body parts.

Move them.

Delete them.

Duplicate them.

Preview the resulting animation.

### Test 7 — Undo and redo

Rotate a bone, move an object, edit a keyframe, change a setting and create a group.

Undo each operation.

Redo each operation.

Verify that the original states are restored accurately.

### Test 8 — Keyboard shortcuts

Test all required shortcuts.

Verify that Shift + F10 opens contextual menus.

Verify that shortcuts do not interfere with text inputs.

### Test 9 — Focused zoom

Hover over a character's hand.

Focus the hand.

Verify that the camera moves toward the hand rather than simply zooming toward the center of the scene.

### Test 10 — Camera independence

Orbit the viewport.

Rotate the character.

Verify that the two operations remain independent.

### Test 11 — Tab suggestions

Select a character and create an animation.

Press Tab.

Verify that relevant suggestions appear.

Preview and apply a suggestion.

Undo it.

Verify that the original animation is restored.

### Test 12 — Workspace controls

Collapse the left panel, right panel and bottom timeline.

Partially expand each.

Resize the panels.

Verify that the main viewport remains usable.

