# FINAL EXPECTATION

I want Stagecraft to feel like a real, intelligent 3D creative studio.

I should be able to hover over a character and immediately understand its structure.

I should be able to click to select and double-click to enter articulated posing.

I should be able to grab an arm, rotate it smoothly and have its joints remain connected.

I should be able to manipulate individual joints, bones, meshes, objects and groups.

I should be able to create sophisticated animation using visible keyframes, curves, paths and editable handles.

I should be able to undo and redo practically every meaningful editing operation.

I should be able to navigate the camera independently, focus on individual details and customize the workspace.

I should be able to press Tab and receive intelligent animation suggestions that help me create better scenes.

A beginner should not need to understand every technical concept before creating something impressive.

The software should guide the user naturally while keeping professional tools available.

**DO NOT JUST MAKE THE INTERFACE LOOK LIKE THIS DESCRIPTION. IMPLEMENT THE ACTUAL INTERACTION AND UNDERLYING SYSTEMS.**

Start by auditing the latest ZIP, identify what already exists, and implement the missing improvements in manageable phases.

Do not remove existing working functionality.

Do not duplicate existing systems.

Do not mark features complete without testing them.

Keep the project buildable and functional after every phase.

Update PROGRESS.md and DECISIONS.md continuously.

If execution limits are reached, preserve the working state and document the exact next task.

The objective is a genuinely powerful, intuitive and intelligent Stagecraft 3D Studio.